    <!-- Terms and disclaimer sheet -->
    <string name="terms_title">Terms and disclaimer</string>
    <string name="terms_use_title">What this app is</string>
    <string name="terms_use_body">Downtify for Android is a free, open-source client for Downtify, a music server you run yourself. It plays and manages the music on your own server. It is not a music service and it doesn\'t host any music.</string>
    <string name="terms_responsibility_title">Your responsibility</string>
    <string name="terms_responsibility_body">You are responsible for the music you search for, download, store and play with Downtify, and for following the copyright laws and the terms of the services involved where you live. Downtify does not support the unauthorized downloading of copyrighted material. Use it only with music you have the right to use.</string>
    <string name="terms_affiliation_title">No affiliation</string>
    <string name="terms_affiliation_body">Downtify is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by Spotify, YouTube, YouTube Music, Deezer, Soulseek or any other service it can find music, previews or artwork through. Their names and logos belong to their owners.</string>
    <string name="terms_warranty_title">No warranty, no liability</string>
    <string name="terms_warranty_body">The app is provided \"as is\", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose. The developers are not liable for any claim, damage, loss of data or legal consequence arising from using it, or from what you do with it. See the license for the full terms.</string>
    <string name="terms_privacy_title">Your data</string>
    <string name="terms_privacy_body">The app has no ads, analytics or tracking, and sends nothing to its developers. It talks to the server you paired it with. Previews, covers, podcast artwork and downloadable fonts come from third-party hosts (such as Spotify, Deezer, podcast publishers and Google), which can see your IP address when you use them. The device token that pairs the phone with your server is kept encrypted on the phone.</string>

